From bf917323edefb0fee246bd2fafe195864511c9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anon <>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:04:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] egl/wgl: ANGLE D3D11 share-handle pbuffers (freedreno d3dkmt)

Implement EGL_ANGLE_surface_d3d_texture_2d_share_handle,
EGL_ANGLE_d3d_share_handle_client_buffer and
EGL_ANGLE_query_surface_pointer for the WGL/CoreWindow EGL driver.

- egl: eglQuerySurfacePointerANGLE entrypoint, driver hooks
  CreatePbufferFromClientBuffer / QuerySurfacePointerANGLE;
  eglSwapBuffers on a pbuffer reaches the driver when the share-handle
  extension is enabled (flush + wait so D3D11 can read it).
- stw: stw_winsys::create_shared_pbuffer / query_shared_texture,
  stw_winsys_framebuffer::get_share_handle; stw_pbuffer_create_shared.
- freedreno d3dkmt winsys: pbuffer backed by one D3D11 MISC_SHARED
  texture (created, or opened from a handle), imported with
  resource_from_handle (LINEAR, pitch align(w*4, 64)).
- Plain pbuffers are shared by default (FD_EGL_PBUFFER_SHARED=0 off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
